# Database migrations (Alembic)

Uses `DATABASE_URL` from `.env` (same as the FastAPI app).

## After you change a model (`src/models/*.py`)

```powershell
# From project root, with venv active:
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe your change"
# Review the new file in alembic/versions/
alembic upgrade head
```

## Common commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `alembic current` | Show applied revision |
| `alembic history` | List all migrations |
| `alembic upgrade head` | Apply pending migrations |
| `alembic downgrade -1` | Undo last migration |

## New empty database

```powershell
alembic upgrade head
```

This applies all migrations and creates tables. You can rely on this instead of `init_db()` for schema setup.

## Existing database (already has tables)

If `upgrade head` says there is nothing to run, your DB is already at the latest revision.
